              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><h3>Annotation</h3><table class=\"hl7__eu__lab__report\"><tr><th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th></tr><tr><td>Renal function is mildly decreased (GFR 63 mL/min/1.73 m²), consistent with stage 2-3a chronic kidney disease. Urine albumin/creatinine ratio is at the upper limit of normal (28 mg/g), suggesting possible early kidney involvement. Recommend monitoring renal function and albuminuria, and addressing cardiovascular risk factors.</td></tr></table></div>"
